Z||000000||Seanh||10-28-2000||01:04 AM||||A while back I replied to a topic about the headlight relays. I mentioned I could get relays for about $3-4 each, alot less then auto part stores sell them for. I said I would get some information on them, and here is all I can really find. They are made by Potter & Brumfield. 40/30 AMP, 12V D.C., The terminals they have on them are: 30, 85, 86, 87, 87A. They are Change-over relays. I can sell them for $3.70 each, it would take me a little time to get them though. Let me know how much interest there is in them, and I can get them ordered soon maybe. I can also get the prewired plug that plug into the back of them also, they are $2.00 each, and have: Pre-wired 24" leads, 2 18 guage wires for coil, 3 14 guage wires for switching.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||4
Z||000001||Carrolles||10-28-2000||02:43 PM||||Seanh,<P>Are these direct plug-n-play or do you need to wire in the new plug?<P>Thanks,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-28-2000||03:27 PM||||If you are thinking of plunging them into the car's existing harness. Then yes, they are plug and play. Here we use them on Remote car starter system, so we need the new harness.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
